## What this predicate means

**A `inherits-from` B** — A inherits properties / slots / values from B.  Distinct from `extends` (which is strict CLASS-level subclassing): `inherits-from` covers prototype inheritance, slot inheritance, dataset inheritance, configuration inheritance — any "A acquires B's properties" relation that doesn't fit class-subclass.

Common shapes:
- A consumer's memory-model inherits-from sandbar's default memory-model (config inheritance)
- A prototype-based instance inherits-from another instance (rather than a class)
- A dataset extension inherits-from a base dataset

